Ported (TypeScript to Rust) into crates/kgraf-orchestrator:
- src/admission.rs (`BudgetBook`): `checkBalance` / `holdReservation`. An
  admitted request holds its estimated cost until its usage is recorded; a
  hold is renewed at half its TTL measured from the stored expiry, so only an
  unrenewed hold lapses. Changed: three caps (per task, per run, per trailing
  hour) instead of one balance; renewal driven by the orchestrator's tick
  instead of a timer per hold; release is an in-memory removal that cannot
  fail.
- src/readiness.rs and the dispatch order in src/orchestrator.rs: readiness
  (credential, MCP reachability, complete tool discovery) before capacity, with
  typed failures (missing credential, missing configuration, permission
  revoked disable; transient counts). capacity.ts's "the slot is the contended
  resource" is realized by `AdmissionGate` inside the single-owner loop, so no
  slot table is needed.
- src/orchestrator.rs (`OrchestratorHandle::steer`, `steer_worker`): steering
  text is persisted before it is acknowledged and injected at the next
  boundary where the transcript accepts it; steering a runtime that cannot
  inject at a tool-batch boundary is refused rather than drained
  (runtime.ts: "draining the queue without this silently drops the user's
  words"). When this was written the worker runtime had no injection point,
  so worker steering was refused; orchestrator steering is delivered as data
  to the next orchestrator model call. The runtime injection point now exists
  (below); routing a worker steer to it is decision 0067's U4.

Ported (TypeScript to Rust) into crates/kgraf-runtime (decision 0067, U3):
- src/inject.rs (`SteerQueue`, `Injector`): the per-run steer queue of
  `InMemoryJobStore.ts` (`enqueueSteerVersioned`, `drainSteers`,
  `restoreClaimedSteers`, `closeAndDrainSteers`) and the boundary drain of
  runtime.ts (`drainAndBuildInjections`, `createSteerPreemptPoll`). Kept:
  FIFO is instruction order; enqueue is refused once the run is not running;
  the drain takes the whole queue; a failed apply restores the failed item
  and its suffix at the queue front; the preempt flag is level-triggered and
  cleared by the drain, never on read; the queue closes when the run ends and
  its leftovers are reported, not dropped. Changed: one process owns the
  queue, so no receipts, replica fences or claim expiry; the idempotency key
  is the inbox id, and a resumed worker seeds it from the transcript's
  `Injected` events; no depth cap (`STEER_QUEUE_MAX_DEPTH`), because decision
  0067 never refuses or drops a message for volume. Not ported: the terminal
  continuation (`StopFinalize`), because a kGraf worker that answered has
  retired; quotes and attachments, which kGraf notes do not carry.
- src/worker.rs: the PostToolBatch and PreemptBoundary injection points, as
  the loop's boundary drain and its interrupt races against the model stream
  and the tool round.
